From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:51:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: ADDRESS FETCH, HTTP from classic Rexx (browser and
 Node)

wasm/web/fetch.cls, written in Rexx over cmdhandler.cls, js.cls (fetch())
and json.cls: .CommandHandler~register("FETCH", ...).  Commands GET / HEAD
/ DELETE url [INTO var], POST / PUT / PATCH url [[JSON] value] [INTO var]
(a word, FROM var, JSON FROM var serialized by json.cls, or the WITH INPUT
lines), SAVE url file, HEADER name [value] / HEADER RESET, TIMEOUT
seconds, STATUS, HEADERS [name], JSON [path] (the body as json.cls reads
it: Directory, Array, string, .JsonBoolean, .nil; a path picks one
value).  Words split by wasm/web/commandwords.cls (.CommandWords:
quotes, FROM, INTO anywhere; shared with DOM); values to
INTO var (a stem gets lines), else to WITH OUTPUT (a body never to the
console).  RC 0; the HTTP status, 1 (no such JSON path) or 2 (no JSON
body) with ERROR; -1 network error, -3 wrong command, -4 SAVE cannot
write, with FAILURE.  Copied into bin-node, preloaded in bin-web.  Test:
wasm/tests/fetch.rex with fetch-server.py (44 checks), in
qualify-node-cli.sh and web-api.py.  Not part of the posted RFE.
